    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0336" n="1794" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">603.4193/8–2351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the United
                        Kingdom </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-08-28T20:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1951—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1203. Ur 1007 Aug 23. Dept expects send msg (text in fol tel)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d179-f1"/> re situation Amers in China to FonMins fol powers: Swed,
                    Nor, Den, Neth, Switz, Indo, Burm, India, Pak and USSR. Msg will go concurrently
                    with or soon after Brit note and memo, without ref to Brit action. However,
                    FonOff may wish to inform particular Govts it understands we are making separate
                    approach.</p>
                <pb facs="0337" n="1795" xml:id="pg1795"/>
                <p>Dept appreciates and accepts offer FonOff instr Brit missions collaborate with US
                    colleagues in various capitals.</p>
                <p>If FonOff has comment on our proposed msg pls inform soonest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d179-f1" n="1" xml:id="d179-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 1204 to London, August 28, was identical, except for the last paragraph,
                    to circular telegram 220, September 4, <ref target="#pg1797">p. 1797</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
